            "short": "Pump forward",
            "sentence": "The right ventricle pumps toward the lungs; the left ventricle pumps toward the body.",
            "why": "Higher ventricular pressure opens outlet valves; closed inlet valves prevent backflow into the atria.",
            "active": [
